1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,330
You're not lazy.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,749
Your brain just hates big tasks.

3
00:00:04,099 --> 00:00:06,467
A huge task feels uncomfortable...

4
00:00:06,817 --> 00:00:09,225
So your brain escapes to something easy.

5
00:00:09,225 --> 00:00:10,401
Like your phone.

6
00:00:10,751 --> 00:00:12,644
Two tiny rules fix this.

7
00:00:12,644 --> 00:00:15,588
And rule two is the one almost nobody

8
00:00:15,588 --> 00:00:16,149
uses.

9
00:00:16,499 --> 00:00:18,519
Rule one: if it takes less than two

10
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:20,125
minutes, do it right now.

11
00:00:20,475 --> 00:00:21,923
Reply to that text.

12
00:00:21,923 --> 00:00:23,569
Wash that cup. Done.

13
00:00:23,919 --> 00:00:25,948
Rule two: never start a big goal.

14
00:00:25,948 --> 00:00:27,865
Start its two-minute version.

15
00:00:28,215 --> 00:00:29,515
Want to read more?

16
00:00:29,515 --> 00:00:30,690
Read one page.

17
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,107
Want to work out?

18
00:00:32,107 --> 00:00:33,600
Just put on your shoes.

19
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,941
Starting is the hardest part.

20
00:00:35,941 --> 00:00:38,430
After that, momentum does the rest.

21
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:41,016
So next time a task feels huge,

22
00:00:41,016 --> 00:00:41,937
remember...

